+# Research consulted
+
+Accessed 2026-08-14 against live, published sources:
+
+- [Broadcom KB 440630: Upgrade sequence and related issues for VCF 9.1](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/440630/upgrade-sequence-and-related-issues-for.html) — confirmed that VCF 5.2.x with SDDC Manager can move to 9.1 after VCF Operations, using lifecycle workflows.
+- [Broadcom KB 314608: Correlating VCF versions with component versions](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/314608/correlating-vmware-cloud-foundation-vers.html) — checked the VCF 5.2.2 source bill of materials used by the inventory.
+- [Broadcom KB 392993: Minimum ESXi hosts for a VCF management domain](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/392993/minimum-number-of-esxi-hosts-required-on.html) — confirmed four ESXi hosts for a single-AZ standard vSAN management cluster.
+- [Broadcom KB 430524: Brownfield imported-domain unsupported NSX path](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/430524/upgrading-a-brownfieldimported-domain-fa.html) — confirmed the documented unsupported NSX 4.2.3-to-9.0.1 brownfield example and the recommendation to wait for 9.1.
+- [Broadcom KB 410435: Unified VCF product release versioning](https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/410435/unified-vcf-product-releases-versioning.html) — confirmed the unified 9.1.0.0 component-version convention used for target declarations.
+- [vmware/vcf-api-specs tag 9.1.0.0](https://github.com/vmware/vcf-api-specs/tree/9.1.0.0/specifications/vcf-installer) — checked the Apache-2.0 VCF Installer OpenAPI source and its `SddcSpec` definition.
